    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d325">

                <pb facs="0652" n="586" xml:id="pg586"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/2244<hi rendition="#superscript"
                    >9/11</hi></note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Japanese Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Nomura</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-02">September 2, 1941</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: Thank you for your letter
                    of August 29 in which you say that your Government “for various considerations
                    feels that secrecy at this time is essential for the success of the
                    conversations”; and that you therefore request my cooperation in this
                    regard.</p>
                <p>I shall be glad to conform to the desires of yourself and your Government in the
                    foregoing respect, to every practical extent.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi></signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
